body:
I can also confirm that reverting this specific change in the current `glslang` fixes the issue:

```diff
diff --git a/thirdparty/glslang/SPIRV/GlslangToSpv.cpp b/thirdparty/glslang/SPIRV/GlslangToSpv.cpp
index 1a5c40c53a..d1f31f18a0 100644
--- a/thirdparty/glslang/SPIRV/GlslangToSpv.cpp
+++ b/thirdparty/glslang/SPIRV/GlslangToSpv.cpp
@@ -5177,12 +5177,12 @@ spv::Id TGlslangToSpvTraverser::createSpvVariable(const glslang::TIntermSymbol*
         }
     }

-    std::vector<spv::Decoration> topLevelDecorations;
-    glslang::TQualifier typeQualifier = node->getType().getQualifier();
-    TranslateMemoryDecoration(typeQualifier, topLevelDecorations, glslangIntermediate->usingVulkanMemoryModel());
-    for (auto deco : topLevelDecorations) {
-        builder.addDecoration(var, deco);
-    }
+    //std::vector<spv::Decoration> topLevelDecorations;
+    //glslang::TQualifier typeQualifier = node->getType().getQualifier();
+    //TranslateMemoryDecoration(typeQualifier, topLevelDecorations, glslangIntermediate->usingVulkanMemoryModel());
+    //for (auto deco : topLevelDecorations) {
+    //    builder.addDecoration(var, deco);
+    //}
     return var;
 }
```

So we probably can just wrap this part in `ifndef __APPLE__` as a hot fix.

I've narrowed it down in the generated shader source, which includes `__restrict` on pointers. For example, the ParticleCopyShaderRD:12 after (with your patch):

```msl
struct spvDescriptorSetBuffer0
{
    device Particles* particles [[id(0)]];
    device Transforms* instances [[id(1)]];
};

struct spvDescriptorSetBuffer2
{
    device TrailBindPoses* trail_bind_poses [[id(0)]];
};
```

and before

```msl
struct spvDescriptorSetBuffer0
{
    device Particles* __restrict particles [[id(0)]];
    device Transforms* __restrict instances [[id(1)]];
};

struct spvDescriptorSetBuffer2
{
    device TrailBindPoses* __restrict trail_bind_poses [[id(0)]];
};
```

That might suggest there are cases where the pointers _do_ alias.
